# cli: optional server password + serve default port
#
# `opencode serve` now serves without authentication by default. Password mode is
# opt-in via `--password` / `-p`, and a bare serve keeps port 4096.
#
#   packages/cli/src/commands/commands.ts
#   packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/serve.ts
#   packages/cli/src/server-process.ts
#   packages/server/src/process.ts
#
# Root cause fixed here: `packages/server/src/process.ts` has an early `dispatch()`
# gate that calls `authorizedRequest()` before the router runs. With no password,
# `ServerAuth.Config` is `Option.none()`, and `ServerAuth.authorized()` returns
# false for that config, so every /api request was rejected with 401 even though
# the HTTP auth layer itself was configured for no password. The static Web UI
# still loaded (it is served before the API), which made the server *look*
# passwordless until the browser called the API. `dispatch()` now skips the gate
# when no password is configured.
